@page "/legend"

<PageTitle>Legend</PageTitle>

<section class="legend-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Knowledge</p>
    <h1>How this RAG works</h1>
    <p>
        Retrieval-augmented generation: the model answers from found policy slices, not from training memory.
        A C# Policy layer can still Deny after the last generated token.
    </p>

    <h2>Pipeline</h2>
    <ol>
        <li><strong>Ingest</strong> — at startup, read <code>data/seed/policy/*.md</code>, split into chunks, embed, store in the index.</li>
        <li><strong>Retrieve</strong> — embed the question, hybrid-search nearest chunks (vector + word overlap).</li>
        <li><strong>Generate</strong> — stream an answer from those chunks only. Citations show as soon as retrieve finishes.</li>
        <li><strong>Policy</strong> — deterministic C# rules. Can Deny or send to a human even if the model said yes.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Terms</h2>
    <dl>
        <dt>Chunk</dt>
        <dd>A short slice of a document, not the whole file.</dd>
        <dt>Embedding</dt>
        <dd>A list of numbers that represents meaning. Similar text sits close together.</dd>
        <dt>Index</dt>
        <dd>The store of chunks + embeddings. This prototype keeps it in memory in the Web process.</dd>
        <dt>Citation</dt>
        <dd>Which source file a retrieved chunk came from.</dd>
        <dt>Stub</dt>
        <dd>A stand-in when Ollama is offline. Not an LLM — copied sentences so the app still runs.</dd>
        <dt>Allow</dt>
        <dd>Grounded answer with citations and no hard conflict.</dd>
        <dt>Deny</dt>
        <dd>Blocked by Policy (secrets, bypass, prohibited gifts, …).</dd>
        <dt>NeedsHuman</dt>
        <dd>Retrieved chunks disagree on a number (refund days, PTO, $ caps).</dd>
        <dt>Refuse</dt>
        <dd>Nothing relevant in the index — the model must not invent policy.</dd>
    </dl>

    <h2>Modules</h2>
    <dl>
        <dt>Ingestion</dt>
        <dd>Turns files into chunks + embeddings. Hosted inside Web.</dd>
        <dt>Assistant</dt>
        <dd>Ask + Policy inside Web. Streams tokens; evals still wait for the final Answer.</dd>
    </dl>
</section>
